<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Otis yr shr falls, div drops.</title>
<headline>Otis yr shr falls, div drops.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Nov 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     50.1	  vs  79.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 38.0	  vs  64.0</p>
<p>    Distrib income	  10.22	 vs  16.28</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   18.19	 vs  30.48</p>
<p>    Tax			  7.97	 vs  14.21</p>
<p>    Interest received	1.14	 vs   1.95</p>
<p>    Turnover		 204.65	 vs 202.40</p>
<p>Div payable Feb 21</p>
<p>on register Feb 7</p>
<p>Full name: Otis Elevator Co Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that it had restructured its workforce in October and had cut 110 jobs, costing the company 2.4 million rand. It added that the restructuring should measurably improve its competitiveness for the future.</p>
<p>Otis said that backlogs of work had remained stable over the year and should continue so for the forseeable future. Increased competition, particularly from new market entrants, would continue to put pressure on margins. But the company said that given reasonable economic growth it expected an earnings improvement for 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
